"answer": "Zoonoses are animal diseases that people can catch [MLP-4055]. Humans can contract these diseases directly from animals or indirectly through the environment [MLP-4055]. Examples include Lyme disease from ticks carried by deer and deer mice, rabies from wild animals or infected dogs, Salmonella from reptiles like turtles and snakes, and toxoplasmosis from handling litter of infected cats [MLP-4055]."
